<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR unchanged for second session.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR unchanged for second session.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were unchanged for the second consecutive session as uncertainties continued to haunt the spot market, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Nobody wants to move. Everything is still very fluid,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>The central bank benchmark rates remained firm, and no rate cut was expected in the near term owing to the still volatile situation in the regional currencies.</p>
<p>PHIBOR is the average swap rates quoted by 20 banks operating in the country.</p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 JULY 24		 JULY 23</p>
<p>    1 W		24  7/8		 24  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		23  1/4		 23  1/4</p>
<p>    1 M		20 11/16		20 11/16</p>
<p>    2 M		18  5/16		18  5/16</p>
<p>    3 M		16  7/8		 16  7/8</p>
<p>    6 M		15  3/4		 15  3/4</p>
<p>    12M		15  1/8		 15  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		25-Jul		  24-Jul</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
